webp-go

internal/vp8ldec (the VP8L decoder) follows the WebP lossless bitstream
specification (RFC 9649) and ports from libwebp, BSD-3-Clause, copyright
Google Inc.: the distance map and prefix-code reading (src/dec/vp8l_dec.c,
src/utils/huffman_utils.c) and the predictor, cross-colour, subtract-green
and colour-indexing inverse transforms (src/dsp/lossless.c). Its license is
in internal/vp8l/LICENSE.libwebp.

internal/vp8dec (the VP8 key frame decoder) follows RFC 6386 and ports from
libwebp: the boolean decoder, header, token and mode parsing, quantizer setup
(src/utils/bit_reader_utils.c, src/dec/vp8_dec.c, tree_dec.c, quant_dec.c), the
intra predictors, inverse transforms and loop filters (src/dsp/dec.c), the
reconstruction order and edge rules (src/dec/frame_dec.c), and the fancy
chroma upsampler and YUV to RGB constants (src/dsp/upsampling.c, yuv.h,
src/dec/io_dec.c). Its tables are shared with the encoder (internal/vp8enc).

The ALPH chunk reader (internal/webp/decode.go) ports libwebp's alpha header
checks and unfilters (src/dec/alpha_dec.c, src/dsp/filters.c).

The encoder's ports (internal/vp8l, internal/vp8enc) are listed in the README.

src/tables.rs holds RFC 6386 tables. The key frame sub-block mode probabilities (PRED_PROB)
come from golang.org/x/image/vp8, which is under this licence:

